      "name": "signing",
      "title": "Signing — the process, not the code",
      "description": "What any signature in the harness must answer, whatever it covers: who signs, what bytes are signed, which signature suites are accepted and who decides that, where the key is kept, which route signs (API or person, by reach), and what a verifier must check and record. Suites are named by the identifiers the standards already define. Signing is done by the parties' own systems; the harness verifies. Read before you add a signature slot, a trust anchor, a verifier, or a process that signs anything.",
